{"inkVersion":21,"root":[["\n",{"->":"stage_test"},["done",{"#f":5,"#n":"g-0"}],null],"done",{"stage_test":["^This is a test of every stage-direction function built so far.","\n","ev","str","^dupont","/str","str","^off_left","/str",{"x()":"enter","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","ev","str","^dupont","/str","str","^left","/str",{"x()":"jump_to","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^<speaker:dupont>Dupont fades in on the left and slides into position.","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str","str","^off_right","/str",{"x()":"enter","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str","str","^right","/str",{"x()":"jump_to","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^<speaker:jeanne>Jeanne fades in on the right and slides into position.","\n","^Notice how, once Jeanne finishes arriving, she's full opacity and Dupont dims slightly -- that's the <speaker:...> command on the line above driving CharacterView's highlight/dim, separate from anything below.","\n",{"->":"test_choices"},{"#f":1}],"test_choices":[["ev","str","^Test switch_mood","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-0","flg":4},"ev","str","^Test turn_around / face","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-1","flg":4},"ev","str","^Test highlight","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-2","flg":4},"ev","str","^Test jump_to_instant / set_depth","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-3","flg":4},"ev","str","^Test fade_to / fade_in / fade_out","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-4","flg":4},"ev","str","^Test exit / re-enter","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-5","flg":4},"ev","str","^Test per-character queue ordering","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-6","flg":4},"ev","str","^Test long text","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-7","flg":4},"ev","str","^Finish test","/str","/ev",{"*":".^.c-8","flg":20},{"c-0":["^ ",{"->":"test_mood"},"\n",{"#f":5}],"c-1":["^ ",{"->":"test_facing"},"\n",{"#f":5}],"c-2":["^ ",{"->":"test_highlight"},"\n",{"#f":5}],"c-3":["^ ",{"->":"test_depth"},"\n",{"#f":5}],"c-4":["^ ",{"->":"test_fade"},"\n",{"#f":5}],"c-5":["^ ",{"->":"test_exit"},"\n",{"#f":5}],"c-6":["^ ",{"->":"test_queue"},"\n",{"#f":5}],"c-7":["^ ",{"->":"test_long_text"},"\n",{"#f":5}],"c-8":["^ ",{"->":"stage_test_end"},"\n",{"#f":5}]}],{"#f":1}],"test_mood":["ev","str","^dupont","/str","str","^worried","/str",{"x()":"switch_mood","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^<speaker:dupont>Dupont's portrait should now show a \"worried\" mood.","\n","^If you haven't added a dupont_worried.jpg to Resources/Portraits/ yet, check the Console -- you should see a clear warning naming the missing file, and Dupont should stay on his neutral portrait rather than going blank.","\n",{"->":"test_choices"},{"#f":1}],"test_facing":["ev","str","^dupont","/str",{"x()":"turn_around","exArgs":1},"pop","/ev","\n","^<speaker:dupont>Dupont just flipped to face the opposite way from before.","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str","str","^left","/str",{"x()":"face","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^<speaker:jeanne>Jeanne is now explicitly facing left, regardless of whatever turn_around would have toggled her to.","\n","ev","str","^dupont","/str",{"x()":"turn_around","exArgs":1},"pop","/ev","\n","^And flipped back, so repeated testing doesn't leave him backwards.","\n",{"->":"test_choices"},{"#f":1}],"test_highlight":["ev","str","^jeanne","/str",{"x()":"highlight","exArgs":1},"pop","/ev","\n","^<speaker:jeanne>Jeanne should have popped slightly, as if she just spoke -- independent of the <speaker:...> dimming, which only changes opacity, not scale.","\n",{"->":"test_choices"},{"#f":1}],"test_depth":["ev","str","^dupont","/str","str","^center","/str",{"x()":"jump_to_instant","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^<speaker:dupont>Dupont snapped instantly to center -- no slide, unlike jump_to.","\n","ev","str","^dupont","/str",0,{"x()":"set_depth","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^Dupont should now render BEHIND Jeanne if they overlap (sibling index 0 = first = furthest back).","\n","ev","str","^dupont","/str","str","^left","/str",{"x()":"jump_to","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^...and back to his spot, this time sliding normally.","\n",{"->":"test_choices"},{"#f":1}],"test_fade":["ev","str","^jeanne","/str",{"x()":"fade_out","exArgs":1},"pop","/ev","\n","^Jeanne fades out completely...","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str",{"x()":"fade_in","exArgs":1},"pop","/ev","\n","^...and back in, both using the default fade duration.","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str",0.4,1.5,{"x()":"fade_to","exArgs":3},"pop","/ev","\n","^Now easing down to 40% transparency over a slow 1.5 seconds -- fade_to gives full control over both target and duration, in seconds.","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str",1,0.5,{"x()":"fade_to","exArgs":3},"pop","/ev","\n","^...then back to fully visible, quickly this time.","\n",{"->":"test_choices"},{"#f":1}],"test_exit":["ev","str","^dupont","/str",{"x()":"exit","exArgs":1},"pop","/ev","\n","^Dupont fades out and leaves entirely. Try picking another option quickly right after this one -- anything targeting \"dupont\" should log a clear warning instead of doing anything, since he's genuinely off screen now, not just invisible.","\n","ev","str","^dupont","/str","str","^left","/str",{"x()":"enter","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^...and here he is again, freshly entered rather than resurrected.","\n",{"->":"test_choices"},{"#f":1}],"test_queue":["^This tests the ordering guarantee itself: two instructions for the SAME character, fired back to back, with no chance to see the first one finish before the second is called.","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str",{"x()":"turn_around","exArgs":1},"pop","/ev","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str",{"x()":"exit","exArgs":1},"pop","/ev","\n","^If the queue is working, Jeanne fully completes the turn (instant) BEFORE her exit fade even starts -- not simultaneously, not skipped.","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str","str","^off_right","/str",{"x()":"enter","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","ev","str","^jeanne","/str","str","^right","/str",{"x()":"jump_to","exArgs":2},"pop","/ev","\n","^And brought back for the rest of the test. Meanwhile, watch Dupont during all of this -- he should be completely unaffected, since queueing is per-character.","\n",{"->":"test_choices"},{"#f":1}],"test_long_text":["^This is a long text with really a lot of words to see what happens when one single lines goes way above the normal length of a single sentence. I add another sentence afterward but on the same line to see what happens. I wonder if i can break stuff doing this. Ok i will switch line now. The line was not long enough to reach the end so I will continue.","\n","^1000001 1000002 1000003 1000004 1000005 1000006 1000007 1000008 1000009 1000010 1000011 1000012 1000013 1000014 1000015 1000016 1000017 1000018 1000019 1000020 1000021 1000022 1000023 1000024 1000025 1000026 1000027 1000028 1000029 1000030 1000031 1000032 1000033 1000034 1000035 1000036 1000037 1000038 1000039. 1000001 1000002 1000003 1000004 1000005 1000006 1000007 1000008 1000009 1000010 1000011 1000012 1000013 1000014 1000015 1000016 1000017 1000018 1000019 1000020 1000021 1000022 1000023 1000024 1000025 1000026 1000027 1000028 1000029 1000030 1000031 1000032 1000033 1000034 1000035 1000036 1000037 1000038 1000039. 1000001 1000002 1000003 1000004 1000005 1000006 1000007 1000008 1000009 1000010 1000011 1000012 1000013 1000014 1000015 1000016 1000017 1000018 1000019 1000020 1000021 1000022 1000023 1000024 1000025 1000026 1000027 1000028 1000029 1000030 1000031 1000032 1000033 1000034 1000035 1000036 1000037 1000038 1000039. 1000001 1000002 1000003 1000004 1000005 1000006 1000007 1000008 1000009 1000010 1000011 1000012 1000013 1000014 1000015 1000016 1000017 1000018 1000019 1000020 1000021 1000022 1000023 1000024 1000025 1000026 1000027 1000028 1000029 1000030 1000031 1000032 1000033 1000034 1000035 1000036 1000037 1000038 1000039. 1000001 1000002 1000003 1000004 1000005 1000006 1000007 1000008 1000009 1000010 1000011 1000012 1000013 1000014 1000015 1000016 1000017 1000018 1000019 1000020 1000021 1000022 1000023 1000024 1000025 1000026 1000027 1000028 1000029 1000030 1000031 1000032 1000033 1000034 1000035 1000036 1000037 1000038 10000